description:
template.tpl's early-consent feature (v1.1.0) reads the axeptio_cookies cookie before the SDK loads and applies its $$googleConsentMode via updateConsentState, with NO check of which project wrote it:

  const cookieValues = getCookieValues('axeptio_cookies');
  ...
  if (parsed && parsed['$$completed'] && parsed['$$googleConsentMode'] ...) {
    updateConsentState(consentModeStates);
  }

Both Axeptio projects on a domain share that cookie name. With the Brands/Publishers switching added in gtm-1m9 (PR #60), a visitor who consented under one product and later loads the other gets the first product's Consent Mode state applied on load. Demonstrated locally: running the real sandboxed source with product=publishers and a cookie applied the cookie's consent while injecting the TCF SDK.

Likely fix: gate the early update on the cookie payload's project matching data.id, if the cookie carries the clientId. Needs a check of what the SDK actually stores in axeptio_cookies first.

Was theoretical before; becomes likely as soon as the customer in gtm-1m9 pilots two projects on one domain.
